### Verification Evidence (2026-08-26)

- Migration `048_go_web_platform_get_started.sql` updated the three exact pristine
  tenant seeds, preserved their distinct `landing_page_slug` values, and returned
  `UPDATE 0` on a second run. Fresh, pristine-upgrade, customized-page, registered-
  section, and idempotency coverage passed against a disposable PostgreSQL database.
- Backend tests, vet, builds, frontend lint/build/policy gates, and all 285 frontend
  tests passed serially. Two unrelated lazy/timeout tests were unstable only during
  the first heavily parallel run and passed in the deterministic full rerun.
- Backend image `sha256:de94801757dccbedc7a172e61451643ca94fe5e24935632347dc638d91b005b5`
  and the production frontend bundle were deployed to the workspace runtimes for
  `cueballcraft`, `home`, and `thewriterco`; every local fail-closed release probe
  returned `decision=proceed`.
- Public-origin verification is still pending deployment: on 2026-08-26,
  `https://skaiacraft.com` and `https://thewriterco.com` passed generic endpoint
  status probes but still returned `Skaia API is healthy` and the legacy
  three-section `Get Started` document. Phase 2 remains blocked until those
  origins serve the verified surface baseline.
- Exact SEO cache keys were purged without a broad Redis flush. No approved permanent
  GWP artwork was supplied, so existing generic defaults and tenant-owned assets
  remain authoritative instead of introducing invented brand assets.
- Module/package manifests, protobuf and WebSocket identities, auth headers, storage
  keys, runtime names, Docker identities, database names, and repository coordinates
  remain phase-2 contracts and were not changed.

